  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Pick the oregano leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Pick the thyme leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Pick the tarragon leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Pick the cilantro leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Pick the parsley leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Finely chop the garlic. Finely chop the whole Thai chile. Juice the lime. Beat the eggs.",
      "secondary_message": "2 sprigs oregano\n3 sprigs thyme\n1 sprig tarragon\n5 sprigs cilantro\n3 sprigs parsley\n2 cloves garlic\n1 whole Thai chile\n1 lime\n8 eggs"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "For the Steak: In a large bowl, mix together oregano, thyme, tarragon, cilantro, parsley, garlic, chile, olive oil, and lime juice until all ingredients are evenly incorporated, then season to taste with salt and pepper. Or, combine all ingredients in a food processor and pulse until an even paste is formed.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Pour herb mixture over steak tips and mix until the steak is evenly coated. Using a fork, pierce each piece of steak on all over. Allow to sit for at least 1 hour, and up to overnight in the fridge.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "When ready to cook, preheat your grill pan or grill to a high heat, then sear steaks until the center of the thickest piece of each steak is 135°F for medium rare, let the steak tips rest while you cook your eggs.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "primary_message": "For the Eggs: In a large non-stick skillet, melt the butter over medium low heat. When butter is melted add the eggs. Cook over medium low heat until eggs are softly cooked and custardy.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "primary_message": "Slice the steak and divide between four plates. Divide the eggs between the plates as well and serve garnished with chopped chives and toast.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
